From ed94d61eb3381b02144ce5825af9bae31de353bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yumi-Lab <nicolas@yumi-lab.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 21:27:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] accel/tcg: add a persistent translation cache for
 user-mode (-tb-cache)

A large guest that does not generate code at run time is translated
once per run, and on a slow 32-bit host that translation dominates
start-up.  Serialise the code generation buffer, which holds the
TranslationBlock descriptors, the generated code and the search data
contiguously, on process exit, and reload it on the next run so that
nothing is retranslated.

The generated code contains absolute host addresses, so the buffer is
mapped at a fixed address when the cache is enabled, and the cache is
only accepted when the environment matches: same emulator binary, same
guest binary, same guest_base and reserved_va, same buffer address and
size, same translation options.  Any mismatch falls back transparently
to normal translation.  Reloaded blocks are relinked through the
regular tb_link_page path; a cache produced by a multi-threaded run
only contains CF_PARALLEL translations, so the flag is set before the
first execution, which also keeps the first clone() from flushing the
reloaded cache.

Enabled with -tb-cache <file> or QEMU_TB_CACHE, user-mode only.
